// leadSync.dg — DRAFT, not deployed, not tested.
//
// This is Deluge, not JavaScript - it must be pasted into and authored
// inside Zoho's Sigma console (Developer Console -> Automate -> Functions
// -> New Function -> "Invoke as REST API": Yes), it cannot be deployed from
// this repo/Catalyst CLI the way the functions/ folder is. Treat this file
// as a starting reference to paste in and adapt, not working source.
//
// PURPOSE (see plan Phase D correction, confirmed by Zoho Marketplace
// support Aug 2026 - "Zoho CRM Extension Development - US DC Requirement &
// Connections Support Query" email thread): replaces functions/liveChatWebhook
// /crmLeads.js's OAuth-based Lead/Task/Signal write for the shared-backend
// extension path. As a REST-API-triggered Function, Zoho generates a unique
// URL + zapikey PER INSTALLING ORG at setup time, and this function runs
// with implicit, tokenless access to that org's own CRM data - no Self
// Client, no refresh token, no per-customer OAuth setup.
//
// CALL DIRECTION (settled - see plan's "Correction" section, revised once
// more after drafting the first version of this file): Engati's webhook
// still points at Catalyst's liveChatWebhook, UNCHANGED - the whole
// webhook_slug-based org-resolution mechanism (plan Phase A) stays exactly
// as built and tested, no new CRM Variable needed for it. It is CATALYST
// that calls THIS function, not the other way around: liveChatWebhook
// (for shared-backend/extension traffic only - legacy dedicated-project
// deployments still use crmLeads.js's OAuth path unchanged) makes one
// plain HTTPS POST here after storing the raw event, passing just
// {userId, displayName}. This function does the Lead/Task/Signal write and
// returns; it does NOT need to know anything about Engati's packet shape,
// Catalyst's Data Store, or any CRM Variable - clean separation, smallest
// possible surface for this Deluge code to get wrong.
//
// (Earlier draft of this file had Engati calling this Function directly and
// this function invokeurl-ing BACK to Catalyst via a CATALYST_WEBHOOK_SLUG
// CRM Variable the admin would paste in. Reversed: it required the admin to
// route two different URLs correctly, and needed an unconfirmed Deluge CRM-
// Variable-read API. This direction reuses only already-proven pieces.)
//
// SETUP (per the linked Zoho help article - see plan/email thread):
//   1. Developer Console -> Automate -> Functions -> New Function.
//   2. Set "Invoke as REST API" to Yes.
//   3. Paste/adapt this logic (Deluge syntax, not JS - see conversion notes
//      inline below for every call that came from crmLeads.js).
//   4. Save - Zoho shows a production URL + zapikey for the CURRENT org.
//      The org's admin needs to find this (Setup -> Developer Hub ->
//      Functions, or wherever Zoho surfaces an installed extension
//      function's REST API details to an org admin - CONFIRM the exact
//      location, not verified here) and paste the full URL into the
//      Settings page's "Lead sync function URL" field (settings.html/
//      settings.js, functions/orgConfigApi - stored as
//      OrgConfig.crm_function_url, treated as a secret: write-only, never
//      echoed back by GET, same principle as the credential fields removed
//      from OrgConfig everywhere else in this migration).
//   5. Engati's own webhook URL is UNCHANGED - still the Catalyst
//      liveChatWebhook URL from the Settings page's first section, exactly
//      as built in plan Phase A/D. Nothing about the admin's Engati
//      Configure-screen setup changes because of this function existing.
//
// WHAT'S DIFFERENT FROM crmLeads.js's LOGIC, deliberately simplified for a
// first draft (Deluge has no npm-equivalent module system, and rewriting
// crmLeads.js's full sophistication - two-layer cache, in-process Map,
// backfill-if-needed name repair, etc. - in Deluge is a separate, larger
// task than this draft attempts):
//   - No in-process/Catalyst-cache layer for "recently created" phone
//     numbers (crmLeads.js's rememberLocally/recallFromCache) - Deluge
//     functions are stateless per-invocation, there is no long-lived
//     process to cache in. Relies on upsertRecords' duplicate_check_fields
//     only. May reintroduce the same "two quick messages create two Leads"
//     race crmLeads.js's comments describe fixing - worth real testing
//     before trusting this in production, same rigor as everything else in
//     this repo.
//   - No separate updateLeadName/backfillIfNeeded name-repair pass - folds
//     into a single upsert. Revisit if placeholder names ("WhatsApp
//     <number>") are seen persisting after a real name becomes known via a
//     later call with a real displayName.
//
// INPUT: a plain JSON object Catalyst constructs itself - {userId, displayName}
// (displayName optional/blank). NOT Engati's raw packet shape - Catalyst
// already parsed that in liveChatWebhook/index.js before calling here.
// CONFIRM the exact variable-binding behavior Sigma gives a REST API
// function for its POST body (this draft assumes a `request` map is
// available, per the fetched help article's code snippets - not verified
// against a real Sigma environment).

devNote = "DRAFT - not tested against a real Sigma environment, adapt field access to what Sigma actually provides for a REST API function's request body";

userId = ifnull(request.get("userId"), "");
displayName = ifnull(request.get("displayName"), "");

digits = userId.replaceAll("[^0-9]", "");

// Web-channel sessions use UUIDs, not phone numbers - skip rather than
// creating junk records. Mirrors crmLeads.js's ensureLeadForPhone guard.
if(digits.length() >= 8 && digits == userId.trim())
{
	phone = "+" + digits;
	fallbackName = "WhatsApp " + digits;
	leadName = displayName != "" ? displayName : fallbackName;

	// Zoho CRM's REST-equivalent "datetime" rejects a plain ISO "Z" suffix -
	// crmLeads.js's zohoDateTime() comment documents the exact failure this
	// caused (INVALID_DATA). Deluge's zoho.currenttime (org timezone) should
	// be safe to use directly, but CONFIRM this against a real Lead write
	// before trusting it - don't assume Deluge's datetime handling matches
	// raw REST's quirks just because it's a different code path.
	nowStamp = zoho.currenttime;

	leadMap = Map();
	leadMap.put("Last_Name", leadName);
	leadMap.put("Phone", phone);
	leadMap.put("Lead_Source", "WhatsApp");
	leadMap.put("WhatsApp_Unread", true);
	leadMap.put("Last_WhatsApp_Message", nowStamp);

	// upsertRecords with duplicate_check_fields does the find-or-create
	// atomically against live data - same reasoning as crmLeads.js's
	// upsertLead() comment re: the CRM /search index lagging writes by
	// several seconds. CONFIRM Deluge's upsertRecords exposes
	// duplicate_check_fields the same way the REST /upsert endpoint does -
	// this is the single most important call in this draft to verify
	// before trusting it.
	upsertResp = zoho.crm.upsertRecords("Leads", leadMap, {"duplicate_check_fields": {"Phone"}});
	leadId = null;
	if(upsertResp != null && upsertResp.get("id") != null)
	{
		leadId = upsertResp.get("id");
	}

	if(leadId != null)
	{
		// Reply Task - mirrors createReplyTask() in crmLeads.js. Owner
		// resolution simplified to the Lead's own Owner (Deluge's implicit
		// CRM access means we can just read it back) rather than
		// crmLeads.js's FALLBACK_TASK_OWNER_ID constant, which was specific
		// to one legacy customer's org and should NOT be reused here - see
		// that file's updated header note.
		leadRecord = zoho.crm.getRecordById("Leads", leadId);
		ownerId = leadRecord != null ? leadRecord.get("Owner").get("id") : null;

		taskMap = Map();
		taskMap.put("Subject", "Reply to WhatsApp message - " + leadName);
		taskMap.put("Status", "Not Started");
		taskMap.put("Priority", "High");
		taskMap.put("Due_Date", zoho.currentdate);
		taskMap.put("What_Id", leadId);
		taskMap.put("$se_module", "Leads");
		if(ownerId != null)
		{
			taskMap.put("Owner", ownerId);
		}
		createTaskResp = zoho.crm.createRecord("Tasks", taskMap);

		// Signal notification - mirrors notifySignal() in crmLeads.js.
		// CONFIRM the signal_namespace: crmLeads.js's was specific to one
		// legacy customer's org-created Signal
		// ("whatsyoo_newwhatsappmessage") - every installing org needs
		// their OWN Signal created by hand (Setup > Experience Center >
		// Signals, Trigger via API) before this call can succeed, same as
		// the legacy setup required. Consider whether this step belongs in
		// the Settings page's instructions once this file is finalized,
		// since it's a real per-org manual step that doesn't go away with
		// this migration. Left as a TODO below - needs the exact Deluge
		// invokeUrl shape confirmed against a real org with a Signal
		// already configured.
	}

	response = Map();
	response.put("ok", true);
	response.put("leadId", leadId);
	return response;
}

response = Map();
response.put("ok", true);
response.put("skipped", "userId is not a plain phone number");
return response;
